WEBVTT

00:21.372 --> 00:22.772
(Ryeo Un)

00:24.143 --> 00:25.983
(Choi Hyun Wook)

00:28.112 --> 00:29.653
(Seol In Ah)

00:34.693 --> 00:36.492
(Shin Eun Soo)

00:44.233 --> 00:48.101
(Twinkling Watermelon)

00:48.102 --> 00:49.201
(Production sponsors)

00:49.202 --> 00:51.042
(Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism, KOCCA)

00:51.043 --> 00:52.071
(All people, organizations, locations, and incidents...)

00:52.072 --> 00:53.101
(in this drama are fictitious.)

00:53.102 --> 00:54.102
(Staff ensured child actors' safety in the filming of this drama.)

01:02.653 --> 01:03.852
Dad! It's cold!

01:04.183 --> 01:05.382
Help!

01:06.053 --> 01:07.183
Mom!

01:11.492 --> 01:12.992
Mom! Dad!

01:16.433 --> 01:18.703
Mom. Look at me.

01:19.703 --> 01:20.762
Dad.

01:22.232 --> 01:23.333
Eun Ho.

01:23.572 --> 01:25.602
Mom. Dad!

01:26.872 --> 01:28.613
Mom. Dad.

01:30.012 --> 01:31.041
Dad.

01:31.042 --> 01:33.943
If Eun Ho and I were both in danger,

01:34.283 --> 01:35.913
which one of us would you save first?

01:36.613 --> 01:38.382
You, of course.

01:39.822 --> 01:41.022
Eun Gyeol.

01:41.652 --> 01:45.223
You're the voice that connects the family to the world.

01:47.732 --> 01:49.033
You're our angel.

01:49.833 --> 01:50.962
Liar.

01:51.962 --> 01:54.232
You couldn't even hear me asking me for help.

01:55.703 --> 01:57.572
You wouldn't even know if I died.

01:59.343 --> 02:03.343
I see. So this is how it feels not to hear any sounds.

02:04.413 --> 02:06.882
It feels like sinking into a deep ocean.

03:17.052 --> 03:19.382
(Episode 5)

03:26.663 --> 03:27.832
What are you doing out here?

03:28.632 --> 03:30.063
Are you watching over me?

03:35.102 --> 03:36.602
You must have been scared earlier.

03:37.503 --> 03:38.542
I'm sorry.

03:39.873 --> 03:41.743
Dad. You can't hear any sounds.

03:42.273 --> 03:44.273
How did you know that I was drowning?

03:44.913 --> 03:46.482
I may not be able to hear sounds,

03:46.642 --> 03:48.382
but I can see you guys.

03:49.683 --> 03:50.852
How?

03:54.052 --> 03:55.392
The Little Mermaid...

03:56.193 --> 03:58.422
gave her voice away to the witch, but in exchange,

03:59.493 --> 04:01.292
she got two legs.

04:02.832 --> 04:05.132
I lost my voice.

04:05.232 --> 04:08.433
So I prayed again and again to the deity. So in exchange...

04:10.403 --> 04:13.743
One, two, three.

04:13.843 --> 04:15.373
I got a third eye.

04:16.813 --> 04:19.842
I can watch you guys and keep you safe wherever you are.

04:19.843 --> 04:21.112
It's the ultimate eye.

04:23.882 --> 04:25.623
Right here. My scar here...

04:26.352 --> 04:28.623
is the proof of that.

04:29.822 --> 04:32.292
He got the scar in exchange for his voice.

04:34.263 --> 04:35.393
Hey, wait.

04:36.763 --> 04:37.932
Watch out! No!

04:40.133 --> 04:41.302
Darn it.

04:47.473 --> 04:49.812
What if the accident that gave him the scar...

04:50.312 --> 04:51.783
took away his hearing?

04:56.213 --> 04:57.682
Goodness.

04:58.122 --> 05:00.422
Hey, what's wrong with you? Are you crazy?

05:00.752 --> 05:01.823
Are you a pervert?

05:03.292 --> 05:04.562
The scar isn't there.

05:05.763 --> 05:06.823
What scar?

05:08.663 --> 05:10.992
The accident he told me about hasn't happened yet.

05:11.432 --> 05:13.602
What scar am I supposed to have?

05:13.903 --> 05:15.333
If I stop the accident from happening,

05:15.672 --> 05:18.042
I may be able to change Dad's fate.

05:18.643 --> 05:21.312
What? Why are you glaring at me?

05:22.042 --> 05:23.542
Why are there lasers coming out of your eyes?

05:26.982 --> 05:28.852
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say right now.

05:29.482 --> 05:30.752
You need to be careful from now on.

05:31.223 --> 05:32.982
Don't get distracted by silly things.

05:33.552 --> 05:34.752
Focus only on me.

05:36.252 --> 05:40.262
You said "from now on." Until when should I listen to you?

05:40.263 --> 05:41.263
Just for a year.

05:41.463 --> 05:42.463
What?

05:42.992 --> 05:44.833
You're going to mooch off me for a year?

05:45.002 --> 05:46.833
How dare you pull a fast one on me?

05:47.163 --> 05:48.232
Just for a year.

05:48.903 --> 05:50.801
Don't leave my sight just for a year.

05:50.802 --> 05:52.672
Don't stay away from me or disappear on me.

05:53.042 --> 05:54.403
Just stay right next to me.

05:54.542 --> 05:57.882
Hey. Did I tell you that I liked Choi Se Gyeong?

05:57.883 --> 05:59.811
How many times must I say you can't like Choi Se Gyeong?

05:59.812 --> 06:01.653
I don't need your permission!

06:03.252 --> 06:05.223
Do what I say just this once. Please?

06:05.653 --> 06:07.783
You just need to be careful this year. Okay?

06:08.122 --> 06:09.653
I'll keep you safe no matter what.

06:09.922 --> 06:12.593
Don't do that. Please. I'm begging you.

06:12.692 --> 06:14.093
You don't have to protect me.

06:14.663 --> 06:16.132
I like women!

06:16.133 --> 06:18.601
You said Eun Ho and I were gifts from the universe.

06:18.602 --> 06:20.962
The universe has shown us the path. This is the divine will!

06:20.963 --> 06:22.931
So just do what I say!

06:22.932 --> 06:25.142
- Gosh. What nonsense is that?
- Watch out for that!

06:25.143 --> 06:26.903
- I'll take care of it!
- Don't run.

06:30.442 --> 06:32.583
The accident definitely happened this year.

06:33.542 --> 06:34.982
What kind of accident was it?

06:35.982 --> 06:37.583
What's the date of the accident?

06:38.283 --> 06:40.723
I must stay glued to him until I find that out.

06:40.883 --> 06:42.122
Shut it.

06:42.422 --> 06:43.791
I didn't say anything yet.

06:43.792 --> 06:45.362
So continue to shut your mouth.

06:50.963 --> 06:52.033
Hey.

06:52.302 --> 06:54.033
Darn it. How dare you?

06:54.533 --> 06:56.002
You'd better not cross this line.

06:56.273 --> 06:59.442
Anything that comes over this line will be twisted, cut, and broken.

07:00.602 --> 07:02.312
- Let's do it together.
- Do what?

07:02.542 --> 07:03.573
The band.

07:04.073 --> 07:06.242
I will give you the best band as a present.

07:06.383 --> 07:08.852
I will make your youth twinkle just like your wish.

07:09.612 --> 07:10.852
But under one condition.

07:15.852 --> 07:18.062
What is it? What's the condition?

07:19.023 --> 07:22.093
Stay exactly where I can see you just for a year.

07:23.963 --> 07:26.463
Grandma!

07:27.002 --> 07:29.232
I will do whatever it takes to change Dad's future.

07:29.903 --> 07:33.343
That's the reason I traveled back in time to 1995.

07:36.773 --> 07:39.583
Choi Se Gyeong. Don't start dating other guys now.

07:39.643 --> 07:41.352
I'll be there starting next semester.

07:42.612 --> 07:45.153
But you're still coming back during school breaks, right?

07:45.523 --> 07:48.252
No. I will never come back to Korea.

07:48.523 --> 07:50.752
Se Gyeong. We must go inside now.

07:52.093 --> 07:54.192
Thank you for coming here to say goodbye today.

07:54.792 --> 07:56.932
Have a safe flight, ma'am. You too, Se Gyeong.

07:59.333 --> 08:00.502
- Let's go.
- Okay.

08:27.223 --> 08:29.093
Hey, did you forget the promise you made to Choi Se Gyeong?

08:29.333 --> 08:30.632
The school festival is next month.

08:30.633 --> 08:33.403
Our band will be disbanded if we don't have enough people.

08:33.562 --> 08:34.972
We need everyone we can get.

08:34.973 --> 08:36.403
Why did you turn away someone who wanted to join our band?

08:36.833 --> 08:38.143
I didn't turn him away.

08:38.273 --> 08:39.541
I just didn't give him an answer yet.

08:39.542 --> 08:41.242
Gosh. You must get him to join us.

08:41.442 --> 08:42.772
We must recruit him no matter what.

08:42.773 --> 08:44.372
You said he was an excellent guitarist.

08:44.542 --> 08:47.042
He keeps looking at me with those burning eyes.

08:47.212 --> 08:48.711
His eyes are about to burn me to death!

08:48.712 --> 08:50.312
He's got a fighting spirit then.

08:50.483 --> 08:52.853
But enthusiasm isn't the source. Romance seems to be it.

08:53.123 --> 08:54.321
What? What did you say?

08:54.322 --> 08:57.653
When he looks at me, I get this cringy feeling.

08:57.822 --> 08:59.762
- Gosh.
- Just accept it, you jerk.

08:59.763 --> 09:01.992
You can glance at him like this then.

09:01.993 --> 09:03.432
You're saying that because it's not happening to you.

09:03.832 --> 09:05.832
There's a saying that it's okay to fight a tiger,

09:05.962 --> 09:07.962
but looking a madman in the eye should be avoided at all costs.

09:08.472 --> 09:10.571
He said he would make you the best band.

09:10.572 --> 09:11.801
- Do you believe that jerk?
- Hey.

09:11.802 --> 09:14.103
How can that crazy guy form a band?

09:16.172 --> 09:18.242
- What? What's going on?
- What is it?

09:18.243 --> 09:19.882
- What's going on?
- Hey.

09:19.883 --> 09:21.412
- Hold on.
- What?

09:21.413 --> 09:22.653
Where are you going? What's going on?

09:22.783 --> 09:23.783
Let me have a sip of your milk.

09:24.582 --> 09:25.653
That's...

09:25.983 --> 09:27.082
That's my milk.

09:27.722 --> 09:29.352
The almighty guitarist, Kang Hyun Yul,

09:29.353 --> 09:30.821
is going to battle someone.

09:30.822 --> 09:32.122
- Kang Hyun Yul?
- Yes.

09:32.123 --> 09:34.393
- Who?
- I have no idea. I need to go now.

09:34.863 --> 09:35.962
What battle?

09:45.572 --> 09:47.273
It's the fourth week of April.

09:47.503 --> 09:52.042
It's the show, "Popular Battle!"

09:54.312 --> 09:55.652
What's he doing here?

09:55.653 --> 09:58.551
Today's battle will decide if there will be a band or not.

09:58.552 --> 10:01.322
The battle of the century will unfold.

10:01.722 --> 10:04.522
I present you the two genius musicians...

10:04.523 --> 10:06.523
who will knock your socks off.

10:07.263 --> 10:10.033
He can create any genre of music with just a bass guitar.

10:10.263 --> 10:12.162
Great King of Musical Tones,

10:12.163 --> 10:13.763
coveted by the independent bands from Hongdae.

10:14.302 --> 10:18.172
The genius bassist, Kang Hyun Yul!

10:34.523 --> 10:35.592
Next.

10:36.292 --> 10:39.792
His vibe is the intro, and his face is the genre.

10:39.993 --> 10:42.663
The mysterious genius guitarist,

10:43.263 --> 10:45.733
Ha Eun Gyeol!

10:48.003 --> 10:49.033
Go!

11:04.952 --> 11:05.983
Let me continue.

11:06.123 --> 11:07.922
I will now go over the rules for today's battle.

11:08.192 --> 11:10.552
One of them will start first.

11:10.653 --> 11:13.162
Whoever goes second must play something from the same genre.

11:13.163 --> 11:14.893
The format is similar to a jam session.

11:15.092 --> 11:17.532
Whoever can't keep up with it will be the loser of the battle.

11:17.533 --> 11:20.462
But if it's a cool jam session, it means they both nailed it.

11:21.733 --> 11:22.972
Let's decide who goes first.

11:24.373 --> 11:26.242
Heads or tails.

11:26.243 --> 11:27.373
- Heads.
- Tails.

11:29.113 --> 11:30.743
Kang Hyun Yul will lead.

11:34.883 --> 11:36.812
Kid, let's do well. Okay?

11:37.253 --> 11:39.653
Let's not try hard. Let's just do well.

11:41.692 --> 11:43.792
How cute. You have no idea who you're dealing with.

11:44.893 --> 11:48.092
I get it. Teenagers aren't scared of anything.

11:50.633 --> 11:52.962
It looks like he's going to make a band for you.

11:53.462 --> 11:55.932
Hyun Yul is the laziest kid I know. How did he get Hyun Yul to do this?

11:57.373 --> 11:58.773
You're that fake Yoon Dong Jin.

11:59.903 --> 12:00.903
Gosh.

12:01.403 --> 12:03.312
You're pretty good for a fake.

12:03.773 --> 12:05.142
I thought you left the band.

12:05.143 --> 12:08.283
Well, you see, this is my hotel.

12:08.812 --> 12:10.451
I see. You'll be out on the street soon.

12:10.452 --> 12:11.552
I heard the band was getting disbanded.

12:11.653 --> 12:13.221
By the way, what kind of style was that?

12:13.222 --> 12:14.353
I've never seen that before.

12:16.792 --> 12:17.822
You're not going to offer me anything?

12:18.893 --> 12:20.993
Gosh, cute. You know how to play hard-to-get too.

12:22.192 --> 12:24.662
Forget it. This is already turning into a hassle.

12:24.663 --> 12:25.862
There's a way for you...

12:25.863 --> 12:27.733
to learn this style and keep your hotel too.

12:36.342 --> 12:37.413
Do you want to know?

12:38.743 --> 12:40.483
You must know some negotiation tactics.

12:41.243 --> 12:43.552
Sure. This is getting interesting.

12:48.123 --> 12:49.123
Tell me. What is it?

12:50.092 --> 12:51.623
Fine. I'm all ears.

12:54.962 --> 12:56.862
Join the band again with the members of Baekwang Band.

12:56.863 --> 12:57.992
It will solve everything.

12:57.993 --> 12:59.932
I have no interest in forming a band...

13:00.663 --> 13:03.133
with Ha Yi Chan or whatever his name is. Darn it.

13:03.672 --> 13:05.403
What if I were to take Yoon Dong Jin's spot?

13:09.613 --> 13:11.571
- You want to take whose spot?
- Yoon Dong Jin's spot.

13:11.572 --> 13:13.742
This happened because I wasn't Yoon Dong Jin.

13:13.743 --> 13:15.113
So I'll take his place.

13:15.483 --> 13:17.712
Well, I can show you what I can do if you don't think I can do it.

13:19.182 --> 13:20.653
You're a brave kid, aren't you?

13:21.253 --> 13:24.492
But do you think you have enough skills to play with me?

13:24.493 --> 13:26.462
It might be too much for a fake to handle.

13:30.893 --> 13:31.962
What's this?

13:35.503 --> 13:37.373
A token of our deal.

13:38.233 --> 13:39.743
You pick the date for the battle.

13:46.013 --> 13:47.212
(Watermelon-flavored Ice Pop)

13:58.052 --> 13:59.863
- He's so good.
- He's amazing.

14:00.863 --> 14:02.133
He's great.

16:13.222 --> 16:15.892
Hey, thank you! Seriously.

16:15.893 --> 16:18.192
Gosh. That was amazing. Thank you.

16:20.633 --> 16:21.873
(School Club Application Form)

16:26.802 --> 16:29.513
I said no. How many times must I say it?

16:29.812 --> 16:32.142
You need at least five students in your club.

16:32.143 --> 16:34.681
Otherwise, I can't approve of your school club, you punk.

16:34.682 --> 16:35.753
Yes, sir.

16:38.922 --> 16:39.982
(Manager Oh Ma Joo, Bassist Kang Hyun Yul, )

16:39.983 --> 16:41.022
(Drummer Lee Si Guk, Keyboard Player No Se Bum)

16:41.023 --> 16:42.052
(Guitarist Ha Eun Gyeol)

16:43.922 --> 16:45.623
- So there are six people.
- Yes.

16:45.863 --> 16:48.763
This form needs your signature as the final touch now.

16:49.033 --> 16:50.133
Please, sir.

17:26.103 --> 17:27.531
Don't be scared. Glare at them.

17:27.532 --> 17:28.833
We must have the upper hand in this power dynamic.

17:35.942 --> 17:38.543
Hey, guys. You're here.

17:39.442 --> 17:41.482
Welcome to The Manipulators.

17:42.353 --> 17:45.383
Gosh. Did you eat, sir?

17:45.682 --> 17:48.221
Darn it. Do you think we're some sacrificial lambs?

17:48.222 --> 17:49.792
- Okay.
- You're the one who lost the bet.

17:49.793 --> 17:52.022
Why must we bear the consequences with you?

17:53.462 --> 17:55.962
His name is Lee Si Guk. He goes by Mangguk.

17:56.333 --> 17:59.102
He looks as if he would play mahjong in Kowloon Walled City.

17:59.103 --> 18:00.863
He has that look, but he goes to church.

18:01.833 --> 18:03.672
Surprisingly, he was born a Christian.

18:11.073 --> 18:13.012
But when his rock spirit is unleashed...

18:24.123 --> 18:25.893
Welcome to the dark world.

18:26.922 --> 18:28.192
A drummer from the dark world.

18:28.762 --> 18:29.762
Gosh.

18:30.333 --> 18:31.462
Calm down, Mangguk.

18:31.762 --> 18:33.232
He's not Yoon Dong Jin,

18:33.403 --> 18:35.603
but it's true that he brought someone as good as him.

18:38.232 --> 18:40.742
His name is No Se Bum. DO is his nickname.

18:41.073 --> 18:42.073
"DO?"

18:45.383 --> 18:46.642
He studied classical piano.

18:46.643 --> 18:48.241
He went to Germany at age 13 to study music,

18:48.242 --> 18:50.011
but he failed and came back. He's an ill-fated genius.

18:50.012 --> 18:51.313
The reason why he failed...

18:54.722 --> 18:55.823
was stage fright.

18:57.123 --> 18:59.363
When he makes a mistake, feels nervous,

18:59.623 --> 19:01.691
or is terrified, his face gets extremely oily,

19:01.692 --> 19:03.231
instead of being sweaty.

19:03.232 --> 19:05.832
That's why his nickname is DO. "Dry and Oily."

19:05.833 --> 19:07.303
In short, DO.

19:08.303 --> 19:10.133
Anyway, a bet is a bet.

19:10.633 --> 19:11.872
So I'll accept it without complaining.

19:11.873 --> 19:14.142
Oh, you must be the brains of the Baekwang Band.

19:14.143 --> 19:15.202
But,

19:16.643 --> 19:18.043
we want to absorb your band.

19:18.643 --> 19:19.942
That's nonsense.

19:20.113 --> 19:22.653
We got approval for the club as First Love Memory Manipulators.

19:24.883 --> 19:27.481
Then change the front man at least.

19:27.482 --> 19:29.622
- What?
- I told you.

19:29.623 --> 19:31.322
We don't use backing tracks.

19:31.323 --> 19:33.392
Hey, you clever one. I was immature back then.

19:33.393 --> 19:34.761
You're not only immature,

19:34.762 --> 19:36.092
but you also don't have what it takes to be the front man.

19:36.093 --> 19:38.332
"I don't have what it takes?" Why do you think that?

19:38.333 --> 19:39.832
I'm the one who made this band.

19:39.833 --> 19:41.702
Honestly, that's not true.

19:42.472 --> 19:44.502
He should take 99 percent of the credit.

19:45.843 --> 19:49.011
He's right. I'll accept it if he's the front man.

19:49.012 --> 19:51.913
I don't even go to this school. I can't do that.

19:51.942 --> 19:54.313
What should I do to make you acknowledge me as the front man?

19:55.242 --> 19:56.282
Tell me.

19:56.613 --> 19:57.613
Hey, Brain.

19:57.883 --> 19:58.952
Hyun Yul.

19:59.123 --> 20:00.181
Si Guk.

20:00.182 --> 20:01.922
What should I do to make you acknowledge me?

20:16.672 --> 20:18.472
("Walking to the Sky")

20:29.083 --> 20:32.352
On snowy nights

20:32.353 --> 20:35.892
I can't help but think about the past

20:35.893 --> 20:39.261
It reminds me of you

20:39.262 --> 20:43.191
- Hidden deep in my heart - Okay. Make it a key higher!

20:43.192 --> 20:45.962
When I was wandering around

20:46.232 --> 20:49.971
In the dark maze

20:49.972 --> 20:53.042
I didn't know

20:53.043 --> 20:56.511
- Why I had to live - Okay. One key higher.

20:56.512 --> 20:59.981
But I could get by each day

20:59.982 --> 21:03.352
Because I had you

21:03.353 --> 21:06.451
I want to give you everything

21:06.452 --> 21:12.092
For you

21:12.093 --> 21:13.422
Even the last piece

21:15.393 --> 21:17.363
Yi Chan, are you okay? Hey!

21:18.663 --> 21:19.902
Hey, get up.

21:19.903 --> 21:21.103
Are you giving up on being the front man?

21:24.103 --> 21:26.403
Darn it. An audition?

21:27.472 --> 21:28.603
An audition?

21:29.113 --> 21:32.212
Why do I have to do an audition in front of them? Why?

21:33.712 --> 21:35.511
A promise is a promise.

21:35.512 --> 21:37.153
So let's practice just one more time.

21:37.353 --> 21:38.482
What if I practice?

21:38.922 --> 21:40.552
You should be able to play...

21:40.553 --> 21:42.222
an instrument at least as the front man.

21:42.823 --> 21:43.922
Is it possible?

21:44.593 --> 21:48.492
You should be able to sustain three high notes at least as a vocalist.

21:49.032 --> 21:51.962
Is it possible to do all that in three days?

21:52.262 --> 21:54.231
It'd be quicker for me to be born again.

21:54.232 --> 21:56.001
Even if you're born again, you'll be who you are now.

21:56.002 --> 21:59.201
Or I could make a son somewhere and bring him.

21:59.202 --> 22:01.442
He would have the same genes anyway.

22:01.573 --> 22:03.512
What if you have a son who is just like you?

22:03.613 --> 22:05.073
My gosh. It's cold.

22:05.313 --> 22:07.913
- Oh, my. Where did it come from?
- It's cold.

22:08.543 --> 22:09.553
Was it you?

22:10.653 --> 22:11.782
What are you doing?

22:12.153 --> 22:13.383
Sorry.

22:14.323 --> 22:17.691
Hey, why don't we hold an audition to pick our own bandmates?

22:17.692 --> 22:19.363
That's it.

22:19.593 --> 22:21.363
What do you mean?

22:21.462 --> 22:24.032
Don't forget that the festival is in next month.

22:26.202 --> 22:27.502
- Ma Joo.
- Yes?

22:28.133 --> 22:29.903
- Don't stop me.
- What?

22:30.133 --> 22:31.432
I'll be born again.

22:32.272 --> 22:33.903
Hey.

22:34.803 --> 22:35.813
Hey.

22:37.512 --> 22:38.512
Yi Chan.

22:39.682 --> 22:40.712
Yi Chan.

22:47.682 --> 22:49.053
No!

23:04.702 --> 23:05.903
I'll teach you.

23:07.143 --> 23:08.172
Teach me what?

23:08.242 --> 23:10.073
Anything. Whatever it is.

23:11.073 --> 23:12.282
Everything you need.

23:15.313 --> 23:16.583
(Sung Moon English)

23:17.613 --> 23:18.682
What's this?

23:19.353 --> 23:20.452
Is this my first birthday party?

23:20.682 --> 23:21.853
Do I get to pick one of these?

23:21.952 --> 23:25.053
Whatever you choose, you must do the other one.

23:26.992 --> 23:28.893
You know...

23:29.232 --> 23:31.092
Are you going to die or something...

23:31.093 --> 23:33.333
if you explain it so that I can understand it from the beginning?

23:34.833 --> 23:35.932
Yi Chan.

23:37.073 --> 23:38.903
Do you want to be the front man that badly?

23:41.272 --> 23:43.373
You saw me almost throwing up blood at the karaoke earlier, right?

23:43.613 --> 23:44.712
Why do you think I did that?

23:45.682 --> 23:48.843
Okay. I got it. I'll help you then.

23:49.482 --> 23:50.852
I'll do a band with you.

23:50.853 --> 23:52.681
I'll teach you how to play guitar. I'll do everything for you.

23:52.682 --> 23:54.553
- In return, you...
- What?

23:54.952 --> 23:55.992
go to college.

23:57.022 --> 23:58.922
Why are you talking about college out of nowhere?

23:59.123 --> 24:00.761
I told you. I'll make money as soon as I graduate.

24:00.762 --> 24:02.022
It's your grandma's wish.

24:07.962 --> 24:09.602
What's this?

24:09.603 --> 24:11.803
It's only a little.

24:11.833 --> 24:15.272
No. I'm already grateful that you let me live here.

24:15.343 --> 24:17.543
I said it was only a little.

24:18.942 --> 24:21.143
This is not for teaching my grandson. It's pocket money.

24:21.442 --> 24:22.653
No.

24:22.813 --> 24:25.782
Think of it as my offering and just take it.

24:26.282 --> 24:29.022
Yi Chan is my dream.

24:29.353 --> 24:31.793
And this is my offering for my dream.

24:36.932 --> 24:40.303
There's a family issue I can't say.

24:40.633 --> 24:44.333
So Yi Chan grew up without knowing parental love.

24:45.432 --> 24:47.502
He got pretty good grades.

24:47.573 --> 24:48.803
But because of me...

24:49.313 --> 24:52.543
He must've thought that this old woman was struggling.

24:53.043 --> 24:56.782
So he kept saying that he wasn't interested in studying.

24:56.952 --> 24:58.682
And that he would make money...

24:58.883 --> 25:00.553
because he'd be better at it.

25:01.522 --> 25:04.293
He thinks that he's being a good grandson.

25:07.192 --> 25:09.792
Running a guesthouse for decades,

25:09.793 --> 25:12.633
I made food and did laundry for college students.

25:13.432 --> 25:16.803
I've put all their graduation caps on my head on graduation day.

25:18.732 --> 25:20.172
But...

25:21.472 --> 25:24.172
I don't have a big dream.

25:25.143 --> 25:28.313
I just want to see my grandson wearing a graduation cap.

25:29.653 --> 25:31.212
That's all I wish for.

25:33.252 --> 25:34.583
Do you think it will come true?

25:41.022 --> 25:44.893
It's not like I'll be accepted just because I want to go to college.

25:45.833 --> 25:47.163
I'll teach you.

25:48.803 --> 25:50.573
You can go to college if you start working hard from now on.

25:52.133 --> 25:54.242
Why? Do you not want to do it?

25:55.373 --> 25:57.672
Hey, you can try at least.

26:02.343 --> 26:04.012
I've been always curious.

26:04.883 --> 26:06.682
Why are you so nice to me?

26:07.853 --> 26:09.593
- What?
- Am I wrong?

26:09.823 --> 26:11.392
You helped me when I almost disgraced myself...

26:11.393 --> 26:12.522
in front of Se Gyeong.

26:12.692 --> 26:14.022
You saved my life.

26:14.222 --> 26:15.962
You said you would make a band for me.

26:16.563 --> 26:19.202
And you want to teach me how to study and play guitar.

26:20.833 --> 26:22.633
Are you doing all this because you don't want to be kicked out?

26:24.472 --> 26:25.472
No.

26:25.473 --> 26:27.873
Then what? Do you want to sell something to me?

26:30.573 --> 26:32.942
You saved my life many times in your previous life.

26:34.982 --> 26:36.012
I did?

26:39.053 --> 26:40.222
You really did.

26:46.722 --> 26:47.863
In the fire.

27:03.043 --> 27:04.143
In the water.

27:05.672 --> 27:06.742
And...

27:10.083 --> 27:11.083
Open your book.

27:12.452 --> 27:14.823
Right now? All of a sudden?

27:20.722 --> 27:22.163
Today is our first day together.

27:23.363 --> 27:25.903
No, please. Grandma!

27:28.103 --> 27:30.432
Grandma, help me!

27:31.403 --> 27:32.672
Read your book!

27:35.643 --> 27:36.671
You're hitting me again?

27:36.672 --> 27:38.442
I like girls.

27:44.113 --> 27:45.113
Look at that.

27:45.114 --> 27:47.482
Hey, what are you guys doing?

27:48.383 --> 27:50.053
- What is it?
- Come here.

27:52.153 --> 27:55.421
- Look.
- "I have a dream that..."

27:55.422 --> 27:56.962
"one day this..."

27:57.333 --> 27:59.201
- "Nation." - "nation..."

27:59.202 --> 28:02.731
"will rise up and live out..."

28:02.732 --> 28:04.502
But why is this "that" here?

28:04.772 --> 28:06.702
You haven't learned about relative pronouns yet?

28:07.103 --> 28:08.442
What? They're relatives?

28:11.972 --> 28:14.511
Ms. Go, why are you crying?

28:14.512 --> 28:17.382
Ms. Go, if others saw you now, they'd think Yi Chan got into SNU.

28:17.383 --> 28:19.082
He'll have no problem becoming a judge or a prosecutor.

28:19.083 --> 28:21.553
Ms. Go, I told you that you didn't have to worry about Yi Chan.

28:37.303 --> 28:39.172
Hi, I'm in New York now.

28:39.803 --> 28:41.442
Have you missed me, even just a little bit?

28:42.043 --> 28:44.112
I was a little sad because you didn't come to the airport,

28:44.113 --> 28:45.843
but I should understand, being the nice person that I am.

28:46.813 --> 28:49.353
I'll write you a proper letter once I'm done organizing my stuff.

28:49.482 --> 28:50.913
I just wanted to let you know I'm doing well.

28:51.653 --> 28:53.853
Now, you have my address. Write me some time.

28:54.182 --> 28:55.222
From Se Gyeong.

29:01.823 --> 29:02.863
PS.

29:03.532 --> 29:06.133
Everyone at school must now know that I've left to study abroad.

29:06.702 --> 29:07.863
I don't have to see it to know...

29:08.363 --> 29:10.432
how happy they must be to have one less person to compete with.

29:12.002 --> 29:15.303
I wonder if anyone is truly sad that I left.

29:20.742 --> 29:22.982
(The 2nd Hongdae Culture Festival)

29:26.653 --> 29:29.492
(Buy and Sell Used Books)

29:54.782 --> 29:55.782
My gosh.

30:25.472 --> 30:26.512
"My left hand is there..."

30:28.512 --> 30:29.553
"solely as support."

31:39.212 --> 31:41.482
What? You're not going walk in and out the door?

31:42.653 --> 31:44.292
I'm sorry about that day.

31:44.293 --> 31:45.522
Today, I'm here to buy some books.

31:49.532 --> 31:50.692
- Hey.
- Oh, hey.

31:51.093 --> 31:52.632
I was just about to head over to the guesthouse.

31:52.633 --> 31:53.701
Where are you coming from?

31:53.702 --> 31:55.802
I was at a bookstore to get some books for Yi Chan. You?

31:55.803 --> 31:57.132
I was at the burger shop over there...

31:57.133 --> 31:58.573
to meet with the festival preparation committee.

31:58.903 --> 32:01.702
After pressuring them and doing a lot of lobbying,

32:01.942 --> 32:04.372
I managed to snag the last slot at the festival.

32:04.373 --> 32:06.981
My gosh. You mean, we'll give the closing performance?

32:06.982 --> 32:08.442
That's right!

32:08.843 --> 32:10.912
Aren't you getting a feeling that it'll go very well?

32:10.913 --> 32:12.782
Oh, my. This is amazing.

32:14.022 --> 32:16.122
- Girls, did you hear the rumor?
- What rumor?

32:16.123 --> 32:17.292
About the new member...

32:17.293 --> 32:19.093
of Baekwang High's band who showed up out of nowhere.

32:19.222 --> 32:21.662
He's a new guitarist Ha Yi Chan recruited.

32:21.663 --> 32:23.162
I heard he was very talented.

32:23.163 --> 32:24.593
Yes, I heard that too.

32:24.762 --> 32:26.602
I heard he saved the band from being disbanded...

32:26.603 --> 32:29.132
and blew everyone away with his amazing guitar skills.

32:29.133 --> 32:31.172
On top of being such a talented guitarist,

32:31.373 --> 32:33.542
he's super handsome too.

32:33.543 --> 32:35.302
- Really?
- Let's go see him at the festival.

32:35.303 --> 32:36.573
- Yes!
- Yes, let's do that.

32:37.272 --> 32:38.912
Ha Yi Chan is very lucky.

32:38.913 --> 32:41.212
He found such a talented new member and managed to save the band.

32:41.942 --> 32:42.951
What's the point?

32:42.952 --> 32:44.481
Se Gyeong is not here. She went abroad to study.

32:44.482 --> 32:46.152
She's not even here to watch him perform.

32:46.153 --> 32:47.252
He's wasting his time.

32:47.383 --> 32:48.452
That's true.

32:50.153 --> 32:51.323
Gosh, I'm hungry.

32:51.992 --> 32:53.093
(Snail Guesthouse)

32:54.422 --> 32:56.191
If he finds out that she left the country to study abroad,

32:56.192 --> 32:57.333
he'll be shocked, right?

32:57.593 --> 32:59.063
Yes, obviously.

32:59.432 --> 33:00.701
He'll be totally devastated.

33:00.702 --> 33:02.432
- What about the band, then?
- He won't bother.

33:02.932 --> 33:04.903
Se Gyeong was the reason he started the band.

33:06.272 --> 33:08.672
But we can finally say that the band is now complete.

33:08.942 --> 33:11.471
I worked so hard to snag the slot for the closing performance.

33:11.472 --> 33:13.883
And he has finally made up his mind to start studying.

33:14.682 --> 33:15.741
If we go back on the decision,

33:15.742 --> 33:18.012
the head of the festival preparation committee will kill me.

33:18.813 --> 33:23.393
But must we let all of Yi Chan's efforts go to waste?

33:25.692 --> 33:26.792
No.

33:26.793 --> 33:27.823
- We won't tell him.
- We won't tell him.

33:42.103 --> 33:44.113
Hey, can't you knock?

33:44.373 --> 33:45.543
Can't you see that I'm studying?

33:46.172 --> 33:48.143
Oh, sorry.

33:52.583 --> 33:53.853
- Hey, Ma Joo.
- Yes?

33:53.952 --> 33:55.021
Why are you here again?

33:55.022 --> 33:58.421
I'm here for your grandma's famous spicy noodles.

33:58.422 --> 34:00.492
Who do you think you are, coming here for noodles whenever you want?

34:00.992 --> 34:03.461
Grandma! No noodles for him!

34:03.462 --> 34:06.462
No, Grandma. I want a double portion!

34:08.232 --> 34:09.232
A double portion?

34:11.032 --> 34:12.103
Here.

34:13.672 --> 34:14.742
I did my homework.

34:23.913 --> 34:26.582
Oh, my. You really solved everything.

34:26.583 --> 34:27.952
Give me my reward as you promised.

34:32.193 --> 34:33.193
Good job.

34:34.393 --> 34:36.023
- What was that?
- You asked for a reward.

34:36.693 --> 34:37.931
Here's my special compliment.

34:37.932 --> 34:39.862
Hey! What am I, a dog?

34:40.103 --> 34:42.062
I finished my homework,

34:42.063 --> 34:44.272
so teach me how to play the guitar!

34:44.273 --> 34:46.241
Come and have some noodles, guys!

34:46.242 --> 34:47.773
Noodles! Come on.

34:48.242 --> 34:51.071
Noodles, I like banquet noodles

34:51.072 --> 34:52.572
(Snail Guesthouse)

34:52.983 --> 34:55.841
I cooked plenty of noodles, so eat as much as you want.

34:55.842 --> 34:57.082
- Okay!
- Okay!

34:57.083 --> 34:58.983
Eat up, Mr. Tutor.

34:59.583 --> 35:02.682
You must've been stressed out, trying to tutor this fool.

35:03.822 --> 35:05.353
Grandma, your grandson is right here.

35:07.193 --> 35:09.193
I am her great-grandson.

35:13.503 --> 35:14.563
Here.

35:15.833 --> 35:16.901
- Can I have some more?
- Thank you.

35:16.902 --> 35:18.373
- Sure thing.
- Hey, Yi Chan.

35:19.373 --> 35:20.802
Are you sure...

35:21.273 --> 35:23.242
Choi Se Gyeong will come to the festival?

35:24.413 --> 35:25.472
Yes, of course.

35:25.742 --> 35:28.043
If I'm well-prepared, she'll surely come to watch the show.

35:28.583 --> 35:29.652
Really?

35:30.552 --> 35:33.722
Then I'll bring everyone from my department.

35:34.152 --> 35:35.721
I heard she was very pretty.

35:35.722 --> 35:37.793
- Hey, I'm coming too!
- Me too.

35:41.592 --> 35:44.233
Now that you've brought her up, I suddenly miss her like crazy.

35:45.032 --> 35:46.631
Shall I go and see her in secret?

35:46.632 --> 35:47.663
- No!
- No!

35:48.233 --> 35:50.502
Gosh, that was gross. What was that, you guys?

35:50.503 --> 35:52.902
Did you have to spit out noodles like that? What a waste.

35:53.072 --> 35:55.401
You promised me you wouldn't see her until the day of the festival!

35:55.402 --> 35:57.071
A man must keep his promises. You know that!

35:57.072 --> 35:58.272
That's right, loser.

35:58.273 --> 36:00.082
If you want to date her, you must play hard to get.

36:00.083 --> 36:01.812
Make a grand entrance like a dark horse...

36:01.813 --> 36:03.182
to impress Se Gyeong!

36:03.813 --> 36:04.882
Like a dark horse?

36:08.023 --> 36:09.382
They do have a point, right?

36:09.992 --> 36:11.922
Well... Yes, I guess.

36:11.923 --> 36:13.092
- Yes.
- For sure.

36:15.092 --> 36:16.293
You can do this, Yi Chan.

36:17.592 --> 36:19.032
Hold out just until the day of the festival.

36:25.333 --> 36:27.002
- Here, have some.
- It's okay. It's all yours.

36:27.003 --> 36:28.202
I'm sorry, Dad.

36:29.072 --> 36:30.612
She left to study abroad.

36:31.173 --> 36:32.313
And...

36:32.373 --> 36:35.643
I moved to the US in 11th grade to study abroad and stayed there...

36:35.983 --> 36:37.682
until I heard he'd passed away.

36:38.313 --> 36:39.923
And she won't come back.

37:27.262 --> 37:28.361
Thank you.

37:28.362 --> 37:30.602
I forgot to bring the key from the US.

37:30.603 --> 37:32.802
For some reason, I didn't want to leave early today.

37:33.972 --> 37:36.672
Anyway, you left a few days ago.

37:36.673 --> 37:38.112
How come you're back already?

37:40.483 --> 37:43.253
I came back for a few days to take care of something urgent.

37:43.353 --> 37:44.382
I see.

38:02.963 --> 38:04.202
I'm sorry, Mom.

38:06.233 --> 38:08.742
I can no longer be the daughter you want me to be.

38:14.242 --> 38:15.282
I'm sorry.

38:16.713 --> 38:17.952
I'm really sorry.

38:21.083 --> 38:22.523
To tell you the truth...

38:27.293 --> 38:28.722
I'm not sorry at all.

38:32.693 --> 38:33.862
I have a bad feeling.

38:34.362 --> 38:35.432
That dream...

38:36.132 --> 38:37.302
I have an ominous feeling.

39:03.632 --> 39:04.762
Why are you still up?

39:05.233 --> 39:07.131
I'm auditioning tomorrow to be the front man,

39:07.132 --> 39:08.163
so I have to practice.

39:10.273 --> 39:11.432
Gosh.

39:16.242 --> 39:18.643
With musical instruments, you simply can't cram the night before.

39:24.552 --> 39:26.052
Why don't you practice singing instead?

39:26.083 --> 39:29.123
I should try my best to keep my promise.

39:30.253 --> 39:31.452
Seriously though.

39:31.853 --> 39:33.051
I'm doing exactly what you taught me.

39:33.052 --> 39:34.423
What's wrong with me?

39:34.663 --> 39:35.822
It sounds so weird.

39:37.262 --> 39:38.262
Hand it over.

39:39.663 --> 39:41.132
Gosh, I'm so frustrated.

39:45.972 --> 39:49.842
It hasn't been tuned in a while, so the wood soaked up moisture.

40:00.952 --> 40:02.052
My gosh.

40:03.293 --> 40:05.023
What can I do to be as good as you?

40:05.222 --> 40:06.862
Learn to talk to the guitar.

40:07.463 --> 40:08.463
"Talk to the guitar?"

40:09.163 --> 40:10.193
Watch.

40:15.862 --> 40:17.503
If you speak from your heart,

40:23.103 --> 40:24.512
it'll also answer from the heart.

40:27.012 --> 40:28.782
Talk sweetly,

40:32.483 --> 40:33.782
and it'll answer sweetly.

40:35.353 --> 40:36.693
If you get angry,

40:46.233 --> 40:47.632
the guitar will get angry too.

40:52.003 --> 40:53.273
If you're excited,

40:56.572 --> 40:57.812
the guitar will get excited too.

40:57.813 --> 40:59.713
My gosh! That was crazy cool.

41:00.282 --> 41:01.782
Oh, my. That's amazing.

41:02.112 --> 41:04.713
You talk to it using your fingers, and it answers in sounds.

41:05.012 --> 41:06.483
In a way, it's like sign language...

41:08.583 --> 41:09.682
Sign language? What about it?

41:12.893 --> 41:14.222
It's similar to sign language.

41:14.623 --> 41:16.623
Hey, that's such a cool analogy.

41:18.663 --> 41:19.862
My gosh.

41:22.463 --> 41:24.502
Technique isn't important.

41:24.503 --> 41:26.103
Your sincerity is what matters.

41:28.202 --> 41:31.472
If the listeners can feel your emotions and sincerity,

41:31.913 --> 41:33.882
you know you're making great music.

41:34.413 --> 41:35.443
Yes, sir.

42:11.782 --> 42:15.022
(Snail Guesthouse)

42:15.023 --> 42:17.622
Ms. Go, can we have more of the rolled omelet?

42:17.623 --> 42:19.991
Yes, here it is.

42:19.992 --> 42:21.023
Here you go.

42:22.722 --> 42:23.862
Thank you.

42:34.443 --> 42:35.603
What is going on here?

42:38.072 --> 42:40.443
Everyone would believe you if you said you two were brothers.

42:52.322 --> 42:54.623
Hey, meet me at the ice cream shop after school.

42:54.963 --> 42:56.123
The ice cream shop? Why?

42:56.523 --> 42:58.262
You asked me to find you a part-time job.

42:58.833 --> 42:59.992
You already found me a job?

43:00.432 --> 43:02.531
I'll let the manager know, so don't be late.

43:02.532 --> 43:04.432
Okay. Good luck with the audition.

43:13.342 --> 43:14.382
Hey.

43:14.813 --> 43:16.012
It's my expression of love.

43:23.222 --> 43:24.821
- More. Yes, that's it.
- Like this?

43:24.822 --> 43:27.662
- Hey, guys.
- Bounce.

43:27.663 --> 43:29.462
- Pull.
- Bounce.

43:29.463 --> 43:31.693
Hey, nice one.

43:34.503 --> 43:35.532
He looks like he's losing his mind.

43:36.233 --> 43:38.472
How could he be in his right mind when Se Gyeong left to study abroad?

43:38.902 --> 43:40.672
I heard she left without even saying goodbye.

43:40.673 --> 43:43.402
Of course, he already lost his mind. You know?

43:44.512 --> 43:45.912
Hey, let's try it once more.

43:45.913 --> 43:49.983
- Okay.
- Bounce.

43:53.552 --> 43:54.722
What did you just say?

43:56.083 --> 43:57.123
Who...

43:58.523 --> 43:59.592
went where?

44:50.342 --> 44:51.342
Go!

44:52.813 --> 44:53.983
Yes!

45:18.032 --> 45:19.103
Gosh, it's so ugly.

45:39.652 --> 45:41.563
(White Night)

46:24.932 --> 46:28.143
Me?

46:37.253 --> 46:38.313
You're looking for a guitar, right?

46:38.913 --> 46:40.923
What kind? Folk? Electric?

46:41.523 --> 46:43.423
- Or classical?
- Folk.

46:43.893 --> 46:44.992
Which one?

46:45.322 --> 46:48.563
A dreadnought with a low saddle.

46:48.822 --> 46:50.262
With a pickup already installed.

46:52.432 --> 46:53.463
I have a good one for you.

46:53.563 --> 46:55.562
I'll go get it now. Give me a moment.

46:55.563 --> 46:56.862
Wait, sir.

46:57.333 --> 46:59.833
Would it be okay if I just took a look at it today?

47:00.472 --> 47:02.003
Today's my first day at my part-time job.

47:03.842 --> 47:05.143
I'll come back and buy it soon.

47:05.413 --> 47:06.472
Sure, no problem.

47:07.612 --> 47:08.912
It's for you, right?

47:08.913 --> 47:11.512
No. I want to get it for my dad.

47:12.452 --> 47:14.023
We're in the same band.

47:14.282 --> 47:17.022
My gosh. Your dad is very cool.

47:17.023 --> 47:18.552
He started a band with his son?

47:21.492 --> 47:23.362
- Feel free to browse around.
- Thank you.

47:33.132 --> 47:34.143
Choi Se Gyeong?

47:35.402 --> 47:37.713
- Oh, this... This is it.
- That's so cool.

47:38.643 --> 47:39.712
- Look at that.
- Isn't that the album?

47:39.713 --> 47:41.582
- This is so pretty.
- It's five dollars.

47:41.583 --> 47:42.782
It suits you perfectly.

47:42.882 --> 47:44.712
- A dollar?
- Seriously? A dollar?

47:44.713 --> 47:45.852
- Shall I just buy it?
- Hold on.

47:45.853 --> 47:48.381
All right. The shoes finally found its perfect owner.

47:48.382 --> 47:49.551
I hope you get a lot of use out of them.

47:49.552 --> 47:51.792
- Are you sure they're authentic?
- Yes, of course.

47:51.793 --> 47:54.063
If you want to make sure, take them to the boutique and ask.

47:54.393 --> 47:55.922
You're selling them so cheap.

47:55.923 --> 47:58.132
- I hope you sell a lot of things.
- Thank you. Have a good day.

48:00.503 --> 48:01.833
This is quite lucrative.

48:02.302 --> 48:03.362
Let's see.

48:07.342 --> 48:08.342
Choi Se Gyeong?

48:11.472 --> 48:13.443
- You are Choi Se Gyeong.
- No, I'm not.

48:18.213 --> 48:19.912
It is you. Don't you know who I am?

48:19.913 --> 48:20.923
Gosh.

48:21.382 --> 48:22.752
Do I have to know who you are?

48:22.753 --> 48:24.922
It's fine even if you don't remember me,

48:24.923 --> 48:27.221
but I must know why you're here.

48:27.222 --> 48:28.292
Can't you see?

48:28.293 --> 48:30.062
I'm selling my stuff at this flea market.

48:30.063 --> 48:32.031
That wasn't my question.

48:32.032 --> 48:33.232
You moved to the US without saying goodbye.

48:33.233 --> 48:34.531
You're not supposed to come back,

48:34.532 --> 48:36.131
but you came back, and you're here now.

48:36.132 --> 48:38.131
What is going on?

48:38.132 --> 48:39.132
Who said...

48:39.402 --> 48:41.072
I wasn't supposed to come back?

48:42.402 --> 48:43.442
What?

48:43.443 --> 48:45.143
Is there a reason I shouldn't come back?

48:46.213 --> 48:47.213
No.

48:52.112 --> 48:53.313
Would you say you're athletic?

48:53.413 --> 48:55.123
"Athletic?" Why?

48:55.983 --> 48:57.322
How fast can you run 100m?

48:57.523 --> 48:58.821
I usually hear lines like this in a drama...

48:58.822 --> 49:00.563
right before they run away.

49:00.923 --> 49:01.992
Bingo.

49:04.333 --> 49:05.463
Pack up quickly!

49:07.333 --> 49:08.333
Pack up.

49:09.032 --> 49:11.402
- You think that'd make me run?
- You'll have to run...

49:11.673 --> 49:13.673
because you want to know why I'm back in Korea.

49:15.202 --> 49:16.372
Pack up everything you see here...

49:16.373 --> 49:18.313
and meet me at the snack shop over there in 30 minutes.

49:18.773 --> 49:19.773
You can do it.

49:19.774 --> 49:21.943
Hey. Darn it.

49:22.313 --> 49:23.342
Shoot.

49:23.612 --> 49:24.782
Hey, what am I supposed to do?

49:26.152 --> 49:28.182
- My goodness.
- Clean this up now!

49:31.393 --> 49:33.722
Yi Chan, that idiot, must be so anxious right now.

49:34.193 --> 49:35.922
Who knows? Miracles can happen.

49:35.923 --> 49:37.631
Come on. Don't talk like an amateur.

49:37.632 --> 49:39.732
Hey, such a miracle cannot happen in three days.

49:39.733 --> 49:41.261
Then why did you say you wanted to audition him?

49:41.262 --> 49:42.262
What a hassle.

49:42.702 --> 49:44.732
Because we need a reason.

49:44.733 --> 49:47.873
A pretext for firing Yi Chan and finding a new front man.

49:48.402 --> 49:50.972
Look at you. You're so clever.

49:54.143 --> 49:55.143
What?

49:55.813 --> 49:57.853
Where's this coming from? Who can sing so well?

50:00.413 --> 50:01.483
- The band room!
- The band room!

50:01.623 --> 50:02.681
Let's go.

50:02.682 --> 50:04.853
I couldn't bring myself to face you

50:08.393 --> 50:13.333
I cried so much

50:15.603 --> 50:20.302
Getting soaked in the rain

50:22.972 --> 50:27.643
Crying in the rain

50:30.813 --> 50:36.182
You in the rain

50:37.552 --> 50:42.523
Picturing a faint image of you

50:44.592 --> 50:49.333
Our last words

50:52.032 --> 50:56.342
And your last words

51:01.413 --> 51:06.882
I love you

51:08.483 --> 51:15.623
I love you

51:15.822 --> 51:23.432
I love you

51:32.373 --> 51:33.413
- You passed the audition.
- You passed the audition.

51:43.253 --> 51:45.591
Hey, thanks.

51:45.592 --> 51:47.023
You got everything, right?

51:47.992 --> 51:49.762
Tell me why you're back in Korea.

51:53.532 --> 51:55.702
I came back because...

51:58.632 --> 52:00.531
I took the flight back to Korea!

52:00.532 --> 52:02.173
- Hey!
- Are we good now? Bye, I'm off.

52:03.402 --> 52:05.942
I never liked you anyway, but you really are the worst.

52:05.943 --> 52:07.881
Don't you feel bad for Yi Chan at all?

52:07.882 --> 52:09.281
You're the reason he started the band,

52:09.282 --> 52:11.612
and he's practicing so hard day and night because of you.

52:11.682 --> 52:13.612
How could you leave without a word?

52:14.052 --> 52:15.982
Was it fun to make a complete fool of him?

52:15.983 --> 52:17.492
Do you feel better about yourself now?

52:18.353 --> 52:19.393
You're right.

52:20.123 --> 52:21.362
I am at fault.

52:24.862 --> 52:27.402
Come on. I'll buy you a cold drink.

52:32.202 --> 52:33.233
Darn it.

52:33.802 --> 52:36.471
You shouldn't have tortured him by giving him hope in the first place.

52:36.472 --> 52:37.511
Upon deciding to study abroad,

52:37.512 --> 52:39.511
you should've told him the truth and made him give up.

52:39.512 --> 52:40.712
Even if you think he's a pushover,

52:40.713 --> 52:42.143
you should still be respectful to him at the very least.

52:42.242 --> 52:44.512
- Am I wrong?
- You're right.

52:44.652 --> 52:47.082
Gosh, what a meanie.

52:47.083 --> 52:48.123
Hey!

52:49.882 --> 52:51.091
I'm talking about you right now.

52:51.092 --> 52:52.123
Exactly.

52:52.253 --> 52:54.923
I feel really bad after hearing everything you just said.

52:55.963 --> 52:58.292
I should meet Yi Chan...

52:58.293 --> 52:59.492
- and apologize in person.
- No!

53:00.492 --> 53:02.163
Do not show up in front of Yi Chan ever again.

53:04.932 --> 53:06.072
So there's something.

53:07.103 --> 53:08.143
What do you mean?

53:08.802 --> 53:10.602
A reason I shouldn't come back.

53:10.603 --> 53:12.241
A reason I shouldn't meet Yi Chan.

53:12.242 --> 53:13.313
Whatever.

53:13.373 --> 53:15.042
Just keep your promise. It's your turn now.

53:15.043 --> 53:17.112
Tell me. Why did you come back?

53:18.083 --> 53:19.753
Are you sure you can handle it?

53:19.882 --> 53:21.821
My story is very unrealistic.

53:21.822 --> 53:23.083
You'll find it hard to believe.

53:24.452 --> 53:25.952
It can't be more unrealistic than mine.

53:27.253 --> 53:28.623
I can handle it. Go ahead and tell me.

53:29.722 --> 53:30.762
I came back to die.

53:31.693 --> 53:34.262
Upon arriving in the US, I found out my dad had another woman.

53:34.603 --> 53:36.931
My mom's like a walking time bomb. She is about to explode.

53:36.932 --> 53:39.333
Very soon, she's going to start drinking again.

53:39.472 --> 53:41.801
Then naturally, she'll become more obsessed with me,

53:41.802 --> 53:43.742
and I'll have to live like her puppet.

53:44.543 --> 53:45.873
So I ran away and came back.

53:46.543 --> 53:47.583
To die.

53:48.342 --> 53:49.413
To put an end to all of it.

53:50.143 --> 53:51.782
- Oh, I just...
- But...

53:53.282 --> 53:54.652
something unexpected has happened.

53:54.923 --> 53:56.052
Something very interesting.

53:57.853 --> 54:00.123
So I'm debating whether I should live a few more days and see.

54:02.492 --> 54:05.733
So don't tell anyone that you saw me.

54:06.163 --> 54:07.193
Unless you want to die.

54:23.543 --> 54:24.652
I'm sorry.

54:31.052 --> 54:32.353
I'm here.

54:34.463 --> 54:35.692
My goodness.

54:35.693 --> 54:38.532
You're always cheerful. Why do you seem so out of it today?

54:38.833 --> 54:40.963
Do you no longer manipulate girls' first love memories?

54:42.733 --> 54:44.832
The girl I had a crush on has moved away.

54:44.833 --> 54:47.502
Oh, right. That girl!

54:47.503 --> 54:49.873
Hey, the girl who just left...

54:50.043 --> 54:52.512
is the one who dropped off the invitation for you.

54:52.612 --> 54:54.182
Did you not see her? You wanted to know who it was.

54:59.112 --> 55:01.452
Hey. Shoot. I don't know her name.

55:01.822 --> 55:04.222
Hey, you! The supply room at Seowon Arts High School!

55:05.293 --> 55:06.322
Hey!

55:14.932 --> 55:16.103
You remember me, right?

55:21.043 --> 55:22.072
This.

55:24.313 --> 55:25.413
Was this from you?

55:34.853 --> 55:36.122
And you wrote this?

55:36.123 --> 55:37.423
(From Se Gyeong)

55:40.893 --> 55:41.963
Why?

55:43.393 --> 55:44.832
Why did you write this fake letter?

55:44.833 --> 55:47.132
I am asking you why you had to make a total fool of me!

55:48.833 --> 55:50.063
Why? Do you think I'm a joke?

55:50.663 --> 55:51.801
Did you think I was pathetic...

55:51.802 --> 55:54.572
for chasing the prettiest girl at your school when I was a nobody?

55:55.342 --> 55:56.673
So you pranked me like this?

55:57.242 --> 55:59.012
Is that why you messed with me like this?

56:01.043 --> 56:02.443
If that's the case, congratulations.

56:02.813 --> 56:03.882
Your prank totally worked.

56:04.112 --> 56:05.452
Thanks to you,

56:06.052 --> 56:08.182
Se Gyeong thinks I'm the biggest loser.

56:09.423 --> 56:10.623
Are you happy now?

56:11.423 --> 56:12.722
Answer me.

56:13.623 --> 56:15.963
It's rude not to answer when someone's talking to you.

56:16.463 --> 56:18.233
Are you happy now?

56:25.132 --> 56:26.632
Hey, it's dangerous. There's a car behind you.

56:27.873 --> 56:29.643
It's dangerous. There's a car right behind you!

56:40.083 --> 56:41.182
Have you lost your mind?

56:41.583 --> 56:43.523
You need to step aside when there's a car behind you.

56:44.052 --> 56:45.552
Do your ears not work?

56:46.923 --> 56:48.722
Are you deaf or something?

56:54.132 --> 56:55.163
Hey.

56:57.163 --> 56:58.373
She's so rude.

57:06.313 --> 57:07.572
Hey, you didn't meet her?

57:08.083 --> 57:09.742
I did.

57:10.012 --> 57:11.152
And I regret meeting her.

57:11.382 --> 57:13.512
- I wish I hadn't met her.
- Why do you say that?

57:14.052 --> 57:15.923
She won't answer any of my questions.

57:16.023 --> 57:18.253
I helped her in the past, but she never once thanked me.

57:18.452 --> 57:20.092
She always ignores me.

57:20.592 --> 57:22.991
I've never seen someone so rude.

57:22.992 --> 57:24.293
Yi Chan, you didn't know?

57:25.193 --> 57:26.193
What?

57:26.492 --> 57:27.733
She can't hear.

58:14.443 --> 58:16.043
Do your ears not work?

58:17.282 --> 58:19.083
Are you deaf or something?

58:24.123 --> 58:25.693
Sir, I'll be right back.

58:53.983 --> 58:55.222
It's so odd.

58:56.182 --> 58:58.252
She clearly told me she never once visited Korea...

58:58.253 --> 59:00.322
until she heard Mr. Viva had passed away.

59:00.552 --> 59:01.793
I came back to die.

59:02.362 --> 59:04.123
- Oh, I just...
- But...

59:06.193 --> 59:07.532
something unexpected has happened.

59:07.762 --> 59:10.063
What is it? What could it be?

59:11.132 --> 59:12.172
It doesn't matter.

59:12.173 --> 59:13.833
I just need to make sure Dad's accident doesn't happen.

59:14.233 --> 59:16.873
Dad, how did you and Mom meet?

59:21.742 --> 59:25.182
I met her in a sign language class when I was 20.

59:25.713 --> 59:27.483
I went there to learn sign language...

59:27.583 --> 59:29.382
and fell in love with your mom the moment I saw her.

59:31.423 --> 59:33.822
Why? Because of her face?

59:34.222 --> 59:37.092
Sure, I thought she looked pretty. But it was because of her voice.

59:38.393 --> 59:39.463
Her voice?

59:40.193 --> 59:43.163
Her sign language gestures looked so pretty.

59:43.663 --> 59:45.873
That's her voice, you know.

59:48.972 --> 59:52.143
Hold on. Dad had to learn sign language...

59:52.643 --> 59:54.643
because he lost his hearing due to the accident.

59:55.682 --> 59:57.181
If I stop the accident from happening,

59:57.182 --> 59:58.713
he won't need to learn it,

59:59.083 --> 01:00:01.353
which means he and Mom won't meet in that class.

01:00:02.382 --> 01:00:03.952
Then Eun Ho and I won't be born...

01:00:04.693 --> 01:00:07.091
Oh, no. I must find Mom no matter what,

01:00:07.092 --> 01:00:08.722
so they can meet sooner.

01:00:20.373 --> 01:00:22.273
Take this. You'll catch a cold.

01:01:25.072 --> 01:01:26.132
I came too late.

01:01:28.443 --> 01:01:29.543
I came too late.

01:01:31.472 --> 01:01:32.543
Se Gyeong.

01:01:32.643 --> 01:01:35.143
Hi. It's been a while, Yi Chan.

01:01:39.313 --> 01:01:41.253
Se Gyeong is back.

01:01:41.983 --> 01:01:44.052
(Bestin Rabbit Thirty Seven Ice Cream)

01:01:47.353 --> 01:01:51.393
(When life gives you lemons, make lemonade.)

01:01:53.032 --> 01:01:55.902
(Special thanks to Park Ho San and Oh Hyeon Gyeong)

01:02:22.992 --> 01:02:27.663
(Twinkling Watermelon)

01:02:27.762 --> 01:02:30.962
If I hadn't let Se Gyeong borrow that T-shirt,

01:02:30.963 --> 01:02:33.301
would I have been the one standing before you?

01:02:33.302 --> 01:02:34.571
Yi Chan, hi!

01:02:34.572 --> 01:02:36.071
Are you really the Choi Se Gyeong I know?

01:02:36.072 --> 01:02:38.212
It's crazy that we have to change the song because of what she said.

01:02:38.213 --> 01:02:39.971
I'll give Se Gyeong everything she wants.

01:02:39.972 --> 01:02:41.412
Is our band a joke to you?

01:02:41.413 --> 01:02:42.841
Fine, then I'll leave.

01:02:42.842 --> 01:02:44.312
Don't do anything you'll regret later.

01:02:44.313 --> 01:02:46.082
If you leave like this, I won't take you back!

01:02:46.083 --> 01:02:48.622
So? Have you found out the reason you're here?

01:02:48.623 --> 01:02:50.982
Forget it. Everything's just a mess.

01:02:50.983 --> 01:02:52.422
Nothing is going my way.

01:02:52.423 --> 01:02:54.892
The moment you arrived here,

01:02:54.893 --> 01:02:57.362
everything started to change.
